            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-0915",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "glibc: glibc: Information disclosure via zero-valued network query"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Calling getnetbyaddr or getnetbyaddr_r with a configured nsswitch.conf that specifies the library's DNS backend for networks and queries for a zero-valued network in the GNU C Library version 2.0 to version 2.42 can leak stack contents to the configured DNS resolver."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-0915",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-0915\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libc6\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-0915](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-0915)\nCalling getnetbyaddr or getnetbyaddr_r with a configured nsswitch.conf that specifies the library's DNS backend for networks and queries for a zero-valued network in the GNU C Library version 2.0 to version 2.42 can leak stack contents to the configured DNS resolver.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-0915**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|libc6||[CVE-2026-0915](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-0915)|\n\nCalling getnetbyaddr or getnetbyaddr_r with a configured nsswitch.conf that specifies the library's DNS backend for networks and queries for a zero-valued network in the GNU C Library version 2.0 to version 2.42 can leak stack contents to the configured DNS resolver."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
